      "content": "This is a deeply nuanced debate without a definitive \"more moral\" answer, as both frameworks prioritize different societal needs. Retributive justice is strongly rooted in the belief that justice requires proportional punishment for the wrong committed, emphasizing state authority and \"just deserts.\" In contrast, restorative justice focuses on the harm done to the victim and community, prioritizing repair, dialogue, and the needs of those affected by the offense.\n\nThe \"better\" foundation often depends on the specific harm and the philosophical lens one is using to define \"justice\" in a given context.",
